    "answers": [
      1824545
    ],
    "content": "<p>Hello, I’m having the following problem: When I try to add my Outlook email address to Thunderbird for Android, I get the error \"Authentication unsuccessful: SmtpClientAuthentication is disabled for the Mailbox.\" This points to a help article that only describes a procedure using PowerShell—requiring domain admin privileges, which I don't have. Setting up the IMAP incoming server seems to work fine, but the outgoing server refuses to connect. This is just a personal account. The configuration is: \nServer: <a href=\"http://smtp.office365.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">smtp.office365.com</a>; \nSecurity: StartTLS; \nPort: 587; \nAuthentication: OAuth 2.0; \nUsername: <a href=\"mailto:mymail@outlook.de\" rel=\"nofollow\">mymail@outlook.de</a>; \nClient certificate: None. \nI also tried the configuration using the server <a href=\"http://smtp-mail.outlook.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">smtp-mail.outlook.com</a> (with otherwise identical settings), but I get the same error. Does anyone have any advice?\n</p>",
